---
title: Contacts schema
description: The openschema/contacts contract — people records shared across apps like Vine, Twig and Tide.
---

`openschema/contacts` describes a person on the user's account: name, email, phone and avatar.
It's queryable structured data, so apps can search and sort it — it is **not** end-to-end
encrypted. See [OpenSchema](/docs/neoworks/openschema) for the model, and [storage](/docs/neoworks/storage) for
how encrypted media differs.

## Fields

```toml
[table.contacts]
columns = [
  { name = "display_name", type = "string" },
  { name = "emails",       type = "array"  },
  { name = "phones",       type = "array"  },
  { name = "avatar",       type = "string" },  # content id of an encrypted blob
  { name = "note",         type = "string" },
]
indexes = [
  { columns = ["user_id", "display_name"] }
]
```

The `avatar` is a content id pointing at an [encrypted media blob](/docs/neoworks/storage), not the
image bytes themselves.

## Scopes

- `contacts:read` — read names, emails, phone numbers.
- `contacts:write` — create and update contacts.

## Querying

```sql
SELECT display_name, emails FROM contacts
WHERE user_id = $auth.id
ORDER BY display_name ASC;
```

